# Form Change Check

## Setup

Evaluate this cell first to install Kino.

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:kino, "~> 0.19.0"}
])
```

## Preferences form

Evaluate this cell after setup. It prepares a preferences form with live change reporting.

```elixir
form =
  Kino.Control.form(
    [
      display_name: Kino.Input.text("Display name", default: "Ada"),
      team:
        Kino.Input.select("Team",
          accounts_api: "Accounts API",
          billing_worker: "Billing Worker",
          customer_portal: "Customer Portal"
        ),
      notify: Kino.Input.checkbox("Notify on deploy", default: false),
      page_size: Kino.Input.number("Items per page", default: 10)
    ],
    submit: "Save preferences",
    report_changes: true
  )

:ok
```

## Status output

Evaluate this cell after the form cell. It shows a live status line below the form:
"No changes yet." until the first edit, then a draft line per reported change
and a saved line per submit.

```elixir
status = Kino.Frame.new()
Kino.Frame.render(status, Kino.Markdown.new("No changes yet."))

team_label = %{
  accounts_api: "Accounts API",
  billing_worker: "Billing Worker",
  customer_portal: "Customer Portal"
}

format_summary = fn data ->
  notify_text = if data.notify, do: "notifications on", else: "notifications off"
  "#{data.display_name} | #{team_label[data.team]} | #{notify_text} | #{data.page_size} per page"
end

Kino.listen(form, fn
  %{type: :change, data: data} ->
    Kino.Frame.render(status, Kino.Markdown.new("Draft: " <> format_summary.(data)))

  %{type: :submit, data: data} ->
    Kino.Frame.render(status, Kino.Markdown.new("Saved: " <> format_summary.(data)))
end)

Kino.render(form)
Kino.render(status)
:ok
```
